title: "pallet-delegated-staking: ignore zero-amount delegations"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      A zero-amount delegation is now a no-op instead of storing an empty Delegation record.
      Before, it left the account marked as a delegator and holding a provider reference,
      which blocked it from registering as an agent.

      delegate_to_agent and migrate_delegation return early on a zero amount, and
      Delegation::update stores nothing for a zero-amount entry: an existing delegation at
      zero is removed and a new one is not created. This holds for both new and existing
      delegators, so nomination-pools' bond_extra at 100% commission keeps working.

      A try-state check also asserts that stored delegations are never zero.
crates:
  - name: pallet-delegated-staking
    bump: patch
